.TH K8S\-RIGHTSIZER\-REPORT 1 "2026-09" "k8s-rightsizer-report" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
k8s-rightsizer-report \- turn live Kubernetes usage into PR-ready requests and limits
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B k8s-rightsizer-report
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads the requests and limits currently set on deployments and the usage
actually observed, recommends new values with headroom, and emits either a
report or a unified YAML diff you can commit.
.PP
Usage comes from metrics-server by default, or from Prometheus (p95 over a
window) or from VerticalPodAutoscaler recommendations.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-n " NS" ", " \-\-namespace " NS"
Namespace to analyse.
.TP
.B \-\-diff
Emit patch YAML instead of a report.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output.
.TP
.BI \-\-prometheus " URL"
Use a PromQL p95-over-time instead of a point-in-time
.BR "kubectl top" .
.TP
.BI \-\-days " N"
Lookback window for
.BR \-\-prometheus .
.TP
.B \-\-vpa
Use VerticalPodAutoscaler recommendations instead of metrics-server.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A report or diff was produced.
.TP
.B non-zero
The cluster or metrics source could not be read.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Report on one namespace:
.PP
.RS
.B k8s-rightsizer-report \-n payments
.RE
.PP
A committable patch, from a fortnight of Prometheus data:
.PP
.RS
.B k8s-rightsizer-report \-n payments \-\-prometheus http://prom:9090 \-\-days 14 \-\-diff
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kubectl (1).
Project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/k8s-rightsizer-report
.UE
